Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a3xx: omit unsafe HLSQ registers from crash dumps

Samsung's exact MSM8226 BSP explicitly excludes nine HLSQ register ranges
from fault-tolerance snapshots because reading them can hang the device.
The current common a3xx register list still includes them. Both normal
crashstate capture and hang_debug dumps use this list before GPU reset.

Remove only those nine ranges, keeping all other snapshot registers and
ring/submit information. This avoids a known unsafe operation while trying
to diagnose/recover a hung GPU; it does not fix the original GPU fault.

Vendor source: LineageOS/android_kernel_samsung_msm8226
Commit: 3fa1853ed5d6c3a8ef5a2fda9822705243bbc256
File: drivers/gpu/msm/adreno_a3xx.c, a3xx_hlsq_registers
Upstream comparison: be0e82b8e0c96649b8bc77a99ab0d185243b7659,
queried 2026-10-15; its a3xx register list still contains these ranges.

The new compositor freeze has no surviving GPU fault trace, so this is an
independently vendor-evidenced defensive fix, not a proven diagnosis of
that freeze. Actual fault recovery still requires device acceptance.
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c
@@ -438,6 +438,7 @@
 	return IRQ_HANDLED;
 }
 
+/* Reading HLSQ registers during a hang can hang the device itself. */
 static const unsigned int a3xx_registers[] = {
 	0x0000, 0x0002, 0x0010, 0x0012, 0x0018, 0x0018, 0x0020, 0x0027,
 	0x0029, 0x002b, 0x002e, 0x0033, 0x0040, 0x0042, 0x0050, 0x005c,
